    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Addresses are printed Modicon-style (00001, 10001, 30001, 40001). Subtract the table base and 1 for the wire address; the manual's exception-code text confirms PDU addresses start at 0."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "ModBus and BACnet Communication Instructions - Armor Models 1250-4000, Series 100 & 101",
    "doc_number": "100305786_2000558371 Rev C",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://assets.lochinvar.com/damroot/Original/10014/100305786_2000558371_Rev%20C_AWH%20Modbus%20Bacnet%20Manual%20(52880).pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 3-6 (Modbus configuration, exception codes), 7-8 (memory map, configuration bits), 18-21 (unit operation, conversions), 22-23 (codes)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Temperatures: the conversion section says the Armor passes temperatures in degrees C and the value must be divided by 10. Scale 0.1 is applied to the temperature registers with 0.1 resolution in the map.",
    "Left out: System/Cascade Setpoint (30004) and Tank Setpoint (40004). The map gives them a 0.5 C resolution while the conversion text says temperatures are C x 10, so their scaling is not settled.",
    "Signed types: inlet, flue and tank temperatures have negative minimums in the map and are listed as INT16; the manual itself only says 16-bit word.",
    "Input registers 30001-30003 and 30026 are packed copies of the discrete inputs; the bit order is not stated, so they are UINT16. Use the discrete inputs instead.",
    "The smaller Armor 151-1000 uses a different manual; see the Knight/Armor map."
  ],
